{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1ejxkLucPjqt8thVTJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: make the fix now and measure the results. Don't hold it for the survey.**\n\n**Why not wait for a survey**\n- You already have behavioural evidence, which beats stated satisfaction. The logs show what customers searched for, that it failed, and why. A survey would tell you customers are frustrated. It wouldn't tell you how to fix it.\n- The cost is small and easy to undo. Three engineer-days is less time than it takes to design, run and analyse a survey.\n- Waiting has a cost. About 340 calls a month take up sales time, and some customers who can't find a part probably order elsewhere without calling.\n\n**Check before building (about half a day)**\n- **Confirm the items exist.** Take a sample of the top zero-result terms and check that the parts are actually in the catalogue under your own or a cross-referenced number. If many aren't stocked, or supplier numbers aren't indexed at all, you have a different problem: adding cross-reference data.\n- **Check for collisions.** Make sure stripping dashes and spaces doesn't merge two different parts, for example \"AB-12-3\" and \"A-B123\". Wrong parts are worse than no results for trade buyers.\n\n**Measure before and after**\n- Zero-result rate, overall and for the top 200 terms\n- Search-to-basket and search-to-order conversion for part-number searches\n- Monthly calls tagged \"can't find part online\"\n- Any increase in returns or wrong-part complaints (to catch false matches)\n\n**For the head of sales**\nTheir instinct to hear from customers is sound. Point it at the next question, not this one. After the fix ships, ask the sales team to note on calls tagged \"can't find part\" what the customer actually typed. That will show the next gap, such as synonyms, descriptions or unindexed supplier numbers, with better evidence than a satisfaction score."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_read_input_tokens":5035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4df0d83-15f6-400b-81a4-98270405a5f0","uuid":"adbc5c65-4898-46a6-b1b9-8742d3c210ec","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:15:01.078Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1ejid15rGBajBLC7Bg"}
